{
  "id": "practice-features-of-quadratics",
  "title": "Practice: Features of Quadratic Graphs",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "Find the turning point of y = (x - 3)^2 + 5.",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "(3, 5)" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "(-3, 5)" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "(3, -5)" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "(-3, -5)" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "In the form y = (x - a)^2 + b, the turning point is (a, b). So the turning point is (3, 5). This is a minimum since the coefficient of x^2 is positive."
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "The line of symmetry of y = x^2 - 8x + 12 is:",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "x = 8" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "x = 4" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "x = -4" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "x = 12" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "The line of symmetry is x = -b/(2a) = -(-8)/(2x1) = 8/2 = 4. Alternatively, factorise: (x-2)(x-6) = 0, roots at 2 and 6, symmetry at x = (2+6)/2 = 4."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "How many times does y = x^2 + 2x + 5 cross the x-axis?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "2" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "1" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "0" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "Cannot tell without plotting" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "c",
      "explanation": "Discriminant = b^2 - 4ac = 4 - 20 = -16 < 0. Since the discriminant is negative, the parabola does not cross the x-axis."
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "The roots of y = x^2 + x - 12 are:",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "x = 3 and x = -4" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "x = -3 and x = 4" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "x = 4 and x = -3" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "x = 6 and x = -2" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "x^2 + x - 12 = (x + 4)(x - 3) = 0. x = -4 or x = 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "A quadratic curve has turning point (2, -1) and passes through (0, 7). Find its equation in the form y = a(x - p)^2 + q.",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "y = 2(x - 2)^2 - 1" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "y = (x - 2)^2 - 1" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "y = 3(x - 2)^2 - 1" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "y = -2(x - 2)^2 - 1" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "y = a(x - 2)^2 - 1. Substitute (0, 7): 7 = a(4) - 1. 4a = 8. a = 2. Equation: y = 2(x - 2)^2 - 1."
    }
  ]
